@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# PROSPECTIVE summary scaffold, generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh.
# TODO: replace the placeholder summaryText/decisionPoint below with the
# actual distilled reasoning behind this PR before committing — see
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps below are real
# (from `git log main..HEAD` on branch issue-488-provenance-ci-job); everything else that
# isn't marked TODO can be left as-is.

ghpull:611 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "ci: dedicated CI job for provenance/backlog SHACL validation" ;
    bl:number 611 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:488 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr611 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:488 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-13T22:23:27+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-29T07:48:12Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr611Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #488 asked for a dedicated CI job so a SHACL shape violation in provenance/backlog data would surface as its own named status check instead of a nonspecific failure buried inside the generic Unit & Integration Tests job. Read ci.yml's existing docs/audit/imf-tests jobs as the pattern to mirror, then identified which cargo test binaries actually SHACL-validate provenance/backlog data by grepping tests/*.rs for shacl usage: provenance_queries.rs (validates provenance/summaries/*.ttl against agentprov-shapes.ttl), backlog_ontology.rs (validates the backlog example snapshot against shapes.ttl), and agentprov_ontology.rs (validates agentprov shapes/fixtures, including negative cases, against agentprov-shapes.ttl). Confirmed the exact command locally (cargo test --test provenance_queries --test backlog_ontology --test agentprov_ontology, 26 tests green) before adding it to ci.yml as a new job named 'Provenance SHACL'." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:611 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr611 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr611Summary agp:decisionPoint session:pr611Decision .

session:pr611Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Included all three SHACL-validating test binaries (provenance_queries, backlog_ontology, agentprov_ontology) in the new job rather than only provenance_queries.rs, which the issue text mentioned by name. agentprov_ontology.rs was initially left out on the reasoning that it validates hardcoded fixtures rather than the live provenance/backlog data files, but on reflection it is structurally the same kind of shape-conformance guard as backlog_ontology.rs (mostly negative-fixture tests plus one real-data conformance test), and the issue's own References section names agentprov-shapes.ttl explicitly — the file agentprov_ontology.rs exists specifically to guard. Adding it costs one flag and no extra compilation since the test binary is already built alongside the others." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered scoping the job to only tests/provenance_queries.rs, matching the issue's illustrative example command literally; rejected because it would leave backlog_ontology.rs's and agentprov_ontology.rs's SHACL violations still buried in the generic test job, which is the exact gap #488 was filed to close." .
